  "href": "fixed_point/fixed_point_kakutani_fixed_point.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Kakutani Fixed Point Theorem</h1>\n<p>Let $C$ be a nonempty convex compact subset of a normed vector space. Let\n$F:C\\rightrightarrows C$ be a correspondence such that:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>for every $c\\in C$, $F(c)$ is nonempty, compact, and convex;</li>\n<li>the graph $\\{(c,d)\\in C\\times C:d\\in F(c)\\}$ is closed.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Then the fixed point set\n$$\n  \\{c\\in C:c\\in F(c)\\}\n$$\nis nonempty and compact.</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
